            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for indirectly, then the Tamil for to monitor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: அறிக்கை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறிக்கை — aṟikkai — \"a report; a statement\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறிக்கை வந்தால் உண்மை தெரியும். aṟikkai vantāl uṇmai teriyum. If the report comes out, the truth will be known."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறிக்கை (aṟikkai) வெளியிடு, to issue a statement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறிக்கை (aṟikkai) is native Dravidian: DEDR 314 lists Tamil aṟi, \"to know\", and aṟikkai, \"notice\": what makes a thing known."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
