        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கணக்கெடுப்பு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கணக்கெடுப்பு — kaṇakkeṭuppu — \"a census; a survey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பத்து ஆண்டுகளுக்கு ஒருமுறை மக்கள்தொகைக் கணக்கெடுப்பு நடக்கிறது. pattu āṇṭukaḷukku orumuṟai makkaḷtokaik kaṇakkeṭuppu naṭakkiṟatu. A population census is held once every ten years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally a taking of the count: எடு, to take, is inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கணக்கெடுப்பு (kaṇakkeṭuppu) is built from kaṇakku, \"an account, a count\", and native eṭuppu, \"a taking up\", from eṭu, \"to take\" (DEDR 851)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
