          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சுமார் — cumār — \"roughly; about\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கூட்டத்துக்குச் சுமார் நூறு பேர் வந்தார்கள். kūṭṭattukkuc cumār nūṟu pēr vantārkaḷ. About a hundred people came to the meeting."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before a number: சுமார் (cumār) பத்து மணிக்கு, at about ten o'clock. In speech it also means so-so."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சுமார் (cumār) is usually traced to Persian shumār, \"counting, number\", which reached Tamil through Hindustani: a figure by rough count."
            }
          ]
        },
